WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.688
The monster yelled from inside the cave.

2
00:00:04.689 --> 00:00:06.661
[g@"We ate the Tang Monk!

3
00:00:06.662 --> 00:00:09.956
So you might as well leave!"@g]

4
00:00:09.957 --> 00:00:16.854
"Oh no!" Bajie fell to his knees and cried.

5
00:00:16.855 --> 00:00:19.762
[g@Wujing wiped tears from his eyes.

6
00:00:19.763 --> 00:00:22.425
"Poor Master."@g]

7
00:00:22.426 --> 00:00:25.122
Wukong frowned at his companions.

8
00:00:25.123 --> 00:00:28.694
[g@"I can't believe you two believe that monster."

9
00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:32.884
He sighed. "Wait here."@g]

10
00:00:32.885 --> 00:00:37.372
The monkey turned into a moth and flew into the cave.

11
00:00:37.373 --> 00:00:41.378
He soon found the Tang Monk tied up in a dark room.

12
00:00:41.379 --> 00:00:44.771
Wukong turned back into himself.

13
00:00:44.772 --> 00:00:47.512
"Wukong!" cried the Tang Monk.

14
00:00:47.513 --> 00:00:52.300
[g@"Shh." The monkey untied the monk.

15
00:00:52.301 --> 00:00:55.094
"We must be quiet."@g]

16
00:00:55.095 --> 00:00:59.998
Wukong recited a spell.

17
00:00:59.999 --> 00:01:06.446
A moment later the sound of snoring drifted into the room.

18
00:01:06.447 --> 00:01:12.023
[g@"My spell put the monster and demons to sleep," said the monkey.

19
00:01:12.024 --> 00:01:15.392
"Let's go."@g]

20
00:01:15.393 --> 00:01:18.893
[g@Wukong and the monk came out of the cave.

21
00:01:18.894 --> 00:01:21.495
Bajie and Wujing were thrilled.@g]

22
00:01:21.496 --> 00:01:26.200
"Master, we thought you'd been eaten," said Bajie.

23
00:01:26.201 --> 00:01:29.298
"I knew he was fine," said Wukong.

24
00:01:29.299 --> 00:01:34.302
"Now I'm going to make sure these villains never bother anyone again."

25
00:01:34.303 --> 00:01:38.952
He pulled out his iron bar.

26
00:01:38.953 --> 00:01:43.296
It grew until it was the size of a very tall tree.

27
00:01:43.297 --> 00:01:50.001
"Stand back," said the monkey.

28
00:01:50.002 --> 00:01:55.123
With one swing Wukong smashed the entire cave.

29
00:01:55.124 --> 00:01:59.750
Rocks exploded and fell on top of one another.

30
00:01:59.751 --> 00:02:04.881
Wukong looked at the rubble and smiled.

31
00:02:04.882 --> 00:02:09.608
Weeks went by, and the travelers arrived in a small town.

32
00:02:09.609 --> 00:02:12.897
Bajie's stomach growled loudly.

33
00:02:12.898 --> 00:02:14.860
[g@Wukong laughed.

34
00:02:14.861 --> 00:02:17.771
"I guess we should look for food."@g]

35
00:02:17.772 --> 00:02:22.739
They saw an old monk walking down a street.

36
00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:25.139
"Kind monk," said the Tang Monk.

37
00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:27.691
[g@"Do you know where we can beg for some food?

38
00:02:27.692 --> 00:02:29.684
We are quite hungry."@g]

39
00:02:29.685 --> 00:02:31.623
[g@The old monk nodded.

40
00:02:31.624 --> 00:02:34.716
"Go to Squire Kou's house.@g]

41
00:02:34.717 --> 00:02:39.892
The squire made a vow to feed ten thousand Buddhist monks.

42
00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:43.446
He will surely give you some food."

43
00:02:43.447 --> 00:02:46.992
He gave the Tang Monk directions to the house.

44
00:02:46.993 --> 00:02:50.497
"Thank you," said the Tang Monk.

45
00:02:50.498 --> 00:02:56.363
The travelers arrived at the squire's gate, and a servant let them in.

46
00:02:56.364 --> 00:03:00.631
The squire's house was very large and fancy.

47
00:03:00.632 --> 00:03:03.489
Squire Kou came outside.

48
00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:06.585
[g@"Greetings," he said with a smile.

49
00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:09.137
"Please come inside."@g]

50
00:03:09.138 --> 00:03:12.992
The travelers sat with the squire in a large room.

51
00:03:12.993 --> 00:03:16.297
A servant brought tea and snacks.

52
00:03:16.298 --> 00:03:19.970
"Thank you for inviting us in, Squire," said the Tang Monk.

53
00:03:19.971 --> 00:03:23.767
"We heard that you made a vow to feed ten thousand monks."

54
00:03:23.768 --> 00:03:25.884
[g@"Yes," said the squire.

55
00:03:25.885 --> 00:03:29.078
"I've made plenty of money during my life.@g]

56
00:03:29.079 --> 00:03:32.081
But I want to do good deeds as well.

57
00:03:32.082 --> 00:03:37.319
I hope to be reborn one day as a bodhisattva or even a buddha."

58
00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:42.462
"Well, Squire," said Bajie, "today's your lucky day!

59
00:03:42.463 --> 00:03:46.691
I can easily eat as much food as ten thousand monks.

60
00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:51.128
[g@So if you feed me, you'll definitely become a buddha!"

61
00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:54.217
Everybody laughed.@g]

62
00:03:54.218 --> 00:03:57.817
"It [i@is@i] my lucky day," said the squire.

63
00:03:57.818 --> 00:04:01.874
"Last night I checked to see how many monks I've fed.

64
00:04:01.875 --> 00:04:07.113
So far I've fed 9,996 monks.

65
00:04:07.114 --> 00:04:11.332
I need to feed only four more in order to fulfill my vow."

66
00:04:11.333 --> 00:04:14.522
[g@A smile spread across his face.

67
00:04:14.523 --> 00:04:17.970
"And there are four of you!"@g]

68
00:04:17.971 --> 00:04:21.805
[g@That evening Squire Kou held a feast.

69
00:04:21.806 --> 00:04:24.716
Everybody in the town was invited.@g]

70
00:04:24.717 --> 00:04:29.246
The travelers sat with the squire and his wife, Lady Kou.

71
00:04:29.247 --> 00:04:34.614
Bajie drooled as he gazed at all of the wonderful food on the table.

72
00:04:34.615 --> 00:04:43.688
"Noodles, buns, mushrooms . . . I don't know what to eat first!"

73
00:04:43.689 --> 00:04:48.597
As they ate, Squire Kou leaned toward the Tang Monk.

74
00:04:48.598 --> 00:04:52.205
"So where are you and your companions going?"

75
00:04:52.206 --> 00:04:55.687
"We're traveling to the Western Paradise," said the monk.

76
00:04:55.688 --> 00:04:59.460
"We're going to fetch the True Scriptures from Buddha."

77
00:04:59.461 --> 00:05:02.219
The squire's eyes lit up.

78
00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:04.687
[g@"You are special guests!

79
00:05:04.688 --> 00:05:09.389
I can't let you leave!"@g]

